Z||000006||TSPalmer||05-31-2001||09:29 AM||||Hey Deca at least you can tell when they are on!  My Mom hit the switch somehow and drove around for a while with them on.  She called my Dad and said "Something is wrong with the turn signals"...  Needless to say Dad got a good laugh out of the impending explanation...<P>------------------<BR>T.Shawn Palmer<BR>'85 SE 4cyl 5spd||||reg||10
Z||000007||DecadenceR||05-31-2001||09:47 AM||||That's okay... <BR>When I was 16 I worked at McDonalds... My 25 y/o manager (a guy) couldn't figure out how to turn the hazards off on his Cavalier. I stood there and laughed at him for a good half hour. My then GF went out and told him how to get them off. Ruined our fun....||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroJoe||05-31-2001||09:53 AM||||Well if the lights are just dimming in unison, that is pretty normal.  If you had alot of power accesories going while the car was not moving, you were pretty much relying on a lot of battery power.  And then having the hazards on takes a lot of juice to power all 8 bulbs at once.  If you had the headlights on too, well thats even more power used up too.<P>I dont think it is anything to worry about.  At least your turn signals/hazards arent as messed up as my sister's blazer, everytime she turns a turn signal on her digital dash flashes along with it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||DecadenceR||05-31-2001||10:26 AM||||Okay, cool.<BR>I am trying to get this in as good of shape as possible, since all my friends with their new camaros and civics and jeeps laugh at me and tell me "Why don't you just get something new?"<BR>I'll show em alllllll.....||||reg||1
